            "Monoclinic system, in fine massive to fibrous aggregates; individual crystals very rare. Prismatic cleavage in the grains, barely visible in the mass; uneven to splintery fracture. Hardness 5.5 to 6; specific gravity 3.2 to 3.4; vitreous to waxy lustre; translucent to opaque; refractive index about 1.67 to 1.70. Violetish blue to lavender, sometimes veined white or pink. Cut as cabochons, beads and small objects; its rarity makes it mainly a collector's stone. It may be confused with sugilite or charoite, from which its composition and refractive index distinguish it.",
